==============================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================
  The registered primary has NO crossing to report, at any kappa.
  Coverage at the argmax starts below nominal at rho=1.2 and stays there,
  so the interval never had nominal coverage to lose. 'The rho at which
  it crosses' is undefined on this point set — a stronger failure than
  the multiple-crossings objection, and a different one.

  NOT a contradiction of A's 96-98% at rho=1.2: that measures coverage
  over the design/domain, this measures it at the recipe the model tells
  you to run. The primary does not say which, and they disagree on the
  verdict. Name the point set before the run.
